# Every text file is checked out with the line ends it was committed with, '\n', on Windows
# too. A precaution taken from Git for Windows' documented default, not from a run of this
# project: its installer sets core.autocrlf to true, which writes '\r\n' on checkout, and Git
# Bash reads a carriage return as part of a command, so a shell script with those ends fails.
* text=auto eol=lf
